// Between Frontiers: rules of influence (phase 4). Contract: crates/bf-sim/src/influence.rs
// (InfluenceRules); design: docs/influence.pt-BR.md. Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0.
//
// DESIGN CHOICES, to balance after phase 6 (the owner's rule: features before balance). Per
// mille throughout.
//
// - Dependence of B on A is the weighted sum of its channels, each a share of B's GDP. Only credit
//   is live; investment, trade and protection are dormant until their fronts exist.
// - Goodwill keeps 917 per mille a year: half in 8 years (0.917^8 = 0.50), the design's
//   half-life. Aid buys a vote only while it lasts and a little after (Kuziemko and Werker 2006).
// - Affinity multiplies: from 500 (opposite regimes, no people in common) to 1500 (same laws, a
//   large community of A's main culture in B); the people term is full at 20 % of B's people.
(
    credit_weight: 1000,
    investment_weight: 1000,
    trade_weight: 1000,
    protection_weight: 1000,
    goodwill_yearly_retention: 917,
    affinity_floor: 500,
    affinity_ceiling: 1500,
    regime_weight: 500,
    people_weight: 500,
    people_full: 200,
    // In a proposal of A that B weighs, A's influence over B adds influence × B's GDP × this.
    proposal_weight: 1000,
    source: "docs/influence.pt-BR.md, sections 2 and 3; Hirschman 1945; Kuziemko and Werker 2006",
)
